"Nonnegativity of the $g$-polynomial of split matroids (https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.35550)\nciteturn7academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Gao, Matthew H. ... Date: Mon Sep 28 16:25:02 2026\n\nWe prove that the $g$-polynomial of every split matroid has nonnegative coefficients, establishing Speyer's conjecture for a class closed under taking minors and containing all paving and copaving matroids. ... The identity follows from the covaluative formula of Ferroni and Schröter together with recurrences for its correction polynomials, derived from Ferroni's enumeration of admissible Delannoy paths for Schubert matroids.\nTitle: Nonnegativity of the $g$-polynomial of split matroids\nAuthors: Alice L. L. Gao, Matthew H. Y. Xie\nDate: Mon Sep 28 16:25:02 2026\n\nWe prove that the $g$-polynomial of every split matroid has nonnegative coefficients, establishing Speyer's conjecture for a class closed under taking minors and containing all paving and copaving matroids. Our proof uses a deletion--contraction identity obtained by constructing an auxiliary split matroid. We first show that every simple, cosimple, connected split matroid $M$ has an element $e$ for which both the deletion $M\\setminus e$ and the contraction $M/e$ are connected. More generally, let $M$ be any connected split matroid of rank $k$ on a ground set $E$ with $|E|\\ge4$. Suppose that $e\\in E$ is such that both $M\\setminus e$ and $M/e$ are connected. For every $v\\in E\\setminus\\{e\\}$, we construct a connected elementary split matroid $N_{e,v}$ of rank $k-1$ on $E\\setminus\\{e,v\\}$ satisfying \\[ g_M(t)=g_{M\\setminus e}(t)+g_{M/e}(t)+t\\,g_{N_{e,v}}(t). \\] Using a fixed total order on $E$, we prescribe the proper cyclic flats of $N_{e,v}$ and their ranks. The identity follows from the covaluative formula of Ferroni and Schröter together with recurrences for its correction polynomials, derived from Ferroni's enumeration of admissible Delannoy paths for Schubert matroids. Since all three matroids on the right have fewer elements, the identity supplies the induction step in the proof of nonnegativity.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNonnegativity of the $g$-polynomial of split matroids - arXiv Combinatorics (https://www.arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/paper/2609.35550v1)\nciteturn7search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; Gao, Matthew H. ... Published: 2026-09-28 | Updated: 2026-09-29 ... We prove that the $g$-polynomial of every split matroid has nonnegative coefficients, establishing Speyer's conjecture for a class closed under taking minors and containing all paving and copaving matroids. ... The identity follows from the covaluative formula of Ferroni and Schröter together with recurrences for its correction polynomials, derived from Ferroni's enumeration of admissible Delannoy paths for Schubert matroids.\n\n## Nonnegativity of the $g$-polynomial of split matroids\n\nAlice L. L. Gao, Matthew H. Y. Xie\n\nPublished: 2026-09-28 | Updated: 2026-09-29\n\nComments: 25 pages\n\nNote:\n\nPublication:\n\nmath.CO\n\nenumeration cyclic flat flat ground set matroid schubert polynomial\n\n# • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\n### Abstract\n\nWe prove that the $g$-polynomial of every split matroid has nonnegative coefficients, establishing Speyer's conjecture for a class closed under taking minors and containing all paving and copaving matroids. Our proof uses a deletion--contraction identity obtained by constructing an auxiliary split matroid. We first show that every simple, cosimple, connected split matroid $M$ has an element $e$ for which both the deletion $M\\setminus e$ and the contraction $M/e$ are connected. More generally, let $M$ be any connected split matroid of rank $k$ on a ground set $E$ with $|E|\\ge4$. Suppose that $e\\in E$ is such that both $M\\setminus e$ and $M/e$ are connected. For every $v\\in E\\setminus\\{e\\}$, we construct a connected elementary split matroid $N_{e,v}$ of rank $k-1$ on $E\\setminus\\{e,v\\}$ satisfying \\[ g_M(t)=g_{M\\setminus e}(t)+g_{M/e}(t)+t\\,g_{N_{e,v}}(t). \\] Using a fixed total order on $E$, we prescribe the proper cyclic flats of $N_{e,v}$ and their ranks. The identity follows from the covaluative formula of Ferroni and Schröter together with recurrences for its correction polynomials, derived from Ferroni's enumeration of admissible Delannoy paths for Schubert matroids. Since all three matroids on the right have fewer elements, the identity supplies the induction step in the proof of nonnegativity.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKybernetika (https://dml.cz/bitstream/handle/10338.dmlcz/152714/Kybernetika_60-2024-5_1.pdf)\nciteturn7search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.5 years ago; known lower bound on its guessing number is 20/3 = 6.¯6 and the previously known best ... In [10] it was conjectured (Conjecture 6.4) that the asymptotic guessing number of a ... 7The authors use the notation χf(G) instead of cpf(G), since the chromatic number of the comple-\nBounds on guessing numbers and secret sharing\n569\nFor comparison, in column 4 of Table 2, we show the weaker bound (strictly except\nfor Q) that can be proven with the same use of the copy lemma but without symmetry\nconditions.\n□\n5. HAT-GUESSING GAMES\nWe discussed hat guessing games in the preliminaries section2.5, here we show our\nresults. Our main result is on an undirected graph called R−with 10 vertices. The best\nknown lower bound on its guessing number is 20/3 = 6.¯6 and the previously known best\nupper bound was 59767/8929 = 6.693 . . .. We get an upper bound 1847/276 = 6.6920 . . .\n(≊6.692028986). The other result is to use our tools to get another proof of a known\nlower bound (for RL, a directed graph) from [1].\nFor the lower bounds on asymptotic guessing number using fractional clique cover\nnumber (definition just below) see [10] by Christofides and Markstr¨om.\nDefinition 5.1. (Fracti